/*
  PDFRender - font model implementation.

  PDF fonts are mapped onto RISC OS outline fonts rather than
  interpreted: simple fonts (Type1/TrueType/MMType1) carry their
  /Widths array and a code -> Latin-1 encoding table for the
  FontManager; Type0 (CID) composite fonts carry /W width ranges and,
  when a /ToUnicode CMap is present, code -> Unicode ranges that are
  folded down to Latin-1.  Type3 fonts are recognised but not
  rendered.  Embedded font programs are never parsed - unknown faces
  fall back through /FontDescriptor flags (fixed pitch / serif) so
  position and measure stay right even when the exact face differs.

  Copyright (c) RISC OS Technologies 2026.
  SPDX-License-Identifier: CDDL-1.0
  Licensed under the Common Development and Distribution License 1.0; see LICENSE.
*/

